<title>JAPAN: Japan ethylene output capacity grows 21,000 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Japan ethylene output capacity grows 21,000 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's production capacity for ethylene grew by 21,000 tonnes to reach an annual 7.061 million tonnes as of end-December 1996, compared with a previous survey in end-August 1995, the trade ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The increase can be attributed to Idemitsu Petrochemical Co Ltd and Tosoh Corp lifting their production capacity, the ministry said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of Japan's output capacity of the 10 main petrochemical products is as follows:</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes, per year)</p>
<p>		   =end-December 1996=	 =end-August 1995=</p>
<p>Ethylene		7,061			 7,040</p>
<p>Low-density</p>
<p>    polyethylene    2,221			 2,247</p>
<p>High-density</p>
<p>    polyethylene    1,330			 1,298</p>
<p>Polypropylene	 2,805			 2,664</p>
<p>Ethylene oxide	  995			   924</p>
<p>Styrene monomer     3,256			 3,175</p>
<p>Polystyrene	   1,559			 1,425</p>
<p>Acetaldehyde	    465			   424</p>
<p>Acrylonitrile	   686			   630</p>
<p>Synthetic rubber</p>
<p>   Styren Butadiene   608			   626</p>
<p>   Butadiene	    310			   303</p>
<p>   Isoprene		83			    83</p>
<p>(Output capacity takes into consideration production halts during maintenance checks. The figures do not include facilities which have not been in operation for over three years, and which are also not due to resume operation in the next six months.)</p>
</text>
